STEP 1c -- fill: 1000 new destinations per batch (evidence/8770/8770-fill-k*.out*,
  tools/8770-fill.sh); count = 2001:db8:8770:1:: rows in `show ipv6 neighbors`, read 5 s after
  each batch
    batch  rate     destinations sent   neighbours   hw /128 rows (per member, all equal)
      1   300 pps        1000               505          505
      2   300 pps        2000              1010         1010
      3    50 pps        3000              1934            -
      4    50 pps        4000              2140            -
      5    50 pps        5000              2150            -
      6    50 pps        6000              1984            -
      7    50 pps        7000              2352            -
      8    50 pps        8000              2632         1904  (hw read ~1 min after nbr)
  The responder answered every NS it saw (204,535 NS, 204,535 NA over the case; all
  multicast; NA latency in the batch-3 capture p50 0.06 ms, max 0.30 ms).
  Two things the fill shows:
  (i) RESOLUTION LOSS ON THE CPU PATH. At 300 pps only ~50 % of answered destinations
      became neighbours, and the misses came in contiguous runs of 110-200 addresses
      (0.4-0.6 s). Each missed address was solicited 3 times and answered 3 times.
      At 50 pps (batch 3, NS/NA captured: p/nd-k3.pcap on tb470):
      852 of 1000 new targets resolved on the first NS, 50 on the second,
      39 on the third, 58 never (3 NS, 3 NA, not learned). One was never solicited.
      So the DUT drops a rate-dependent share of valid NAs.
  (ii) EVICTION, NOT REFUSAL, near 2.1 K. Batch 4 kept only 1260 of batch 3's 1934
      entries and 719 of batch 2's 1010. From batch 4 on the count wandered 1984-2632 while
      the DUT re-solicited old entries at a high rate (9344 NS in batch 4 alone).
      (IPv4, T6057, is the opposite: it refuses new entries at 2045.)
  Sandwich read with no new destinations (17:51, nbr -> hw -> nbr, 8770-s2-sandwich.out.gz):
      nbr 1098 / hw 905 on each member / nbr 1098. Every hw row was a learned neighbour.
      193 learned neighbours had NO hw row, although no "Table full" is in the retained log
      before 04:54 UTC. Their ND state is not shown by this CLI. OBSERVATION, not graded.

