STEP 2 -- learned neighbours in hardware (`show platform table ipv6`, `show log`)
  - Up to capacity: YES. Every hw /128 row matched a learned neighbour (10/10 at the
    start; the members' tables were identical at every read).
  - At load: NO. 3030 learned vs 1567 in hardware (B). The first "Table full" retained in
    `show log` is at 04:54:02 UTC (end of run A); there are 3718 in all (IE520-stk
    180/142/1692, -1 146/126/613, -4 133/104/582 in minutes 04:54/55/56), covering 1893
    distinct neighbour addresses, e.g.
      2026 Sep 30 04:56:59 local6.warning IE520-stk-4 EXFX[681]: Unable to add NH Route
      entry nh=2001:db8:8770:1::1:4bd/128 mac=0287.7001.04bd vid:3971 port=port3.0.13.
      Table full
    (8770-s3-log.out.gz, 8770-s3-tablefull.out.gz). The buffer may have rolled; earlier
    messages cannot be ruled out.
  - Maximum hw /128 rows seen: 1904 per member (batch 8).
  -> Step 2 FAILS as written: learned neighbours are not all in hardware, and the hardware
     maximum (~1.9 K) is far below the case's ~5000.

